WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.000
One piece of paper rules the world. Why does everyone want dollars?

00:06.000 --> 00:14.000
In 1944, forty-four nations made a deal: every currency pegged to the dollar — and the dollar pegged to gold.

00:14.000 --> 00:23.000
Then habit took over. Today the dollar sits on one side of eighty-nine percent of all currency trades. Everyone uses it — so everyone must.

00:23.000 --> 00:32.000
In 1974, oil sealed the system. Buy energy, pay in dollars. Need energy? First — earn dollars.

00:32.000 --> 00:41.000
And when panic hits, the world runs to one vault: US Treasuries. Deep. Liquid. Trusted. Fifty-seven percent of global reserves still sit in dollars.

00:41.000 --> 00:50.000
That makes the dollar power — payments can be switched off. Rivals are rising, but slowly. There is still no successor.

00:50.000 --> 01:00.000
So no — it isn't backed by gold anymore. It's backed by trust, habit, and eighty years of network. That's why the dollar rules.
